    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "$$\\begin{array}{r} 2P4\\\\ +\\ \\ Q5\\\\ +\\ \\ R7\\\\ \\hline 406\\end{array}$$\nIn the given addition sum, each letter stands for a different digit from 0 to 9. Which of the following values is not a possible value for $R$?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "1"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "6"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "8"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "9"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Column addition",
        "body": "Units: $4+5+7=16$, carry 1. Hundreds: the sum ends in 4, so exactly 2 is carried from the tens column. Tens: $1+P+Q+R=20$, so $P+Q+R=19$. If $R=1$ then $P+Q=18$, forcing $P=Q=9$, not allowed (different digits). Other values work: $R=3$: $P,Q=7,9$; $R=6$: $4,9$; $R=8$: $2,9$; $R=9$: $4,6$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 1**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "arithmetic",
      "logic"
    ],
    "difficulty": 2,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null
  },
  {
