        "text": "$72^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$100^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$54^\\circ$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Isosceles triangles",
        "body": "Each interior angle of the pentagon is $108^\\circ$. Triangle $CBD$ is isosceles with apex angle $108^\\circ$, so $\\angle CDB=\\frac12(180^\\circ-108^\\circ)=36^\\circ$; likewise $\\angle DCE=36^\\circ$. In triangle $DFC$: $\\angle DFC=180^\\circ-36^\\circ-36^\\circ=108^\\circ$.\n\n**Answer: (B) $108^\\circ$**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
