    "prompt": "In the given diagram $ABCD$ is a square with sides $7\\sqrt2$ cm. $E$ is a point on $DC$ such that $EC=2\\sqrt2$ cm and angle $CFE=90^\\circ$. The area of $AFED$ in cm$^2$ is",
    "image": "qimages/samf/senior-2002-r1/q14.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "49"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "7"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "45"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "47"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Subtract a small triangle",
        "body": "Triangle $ACD$ is half the square: $\\frac12(7\\sqrt2)^2=49$. Triangle $EFC$ has a right angle at $F$ and $\\angle FCE=45^\\circ$, so it is isosceles with hypotenuse $EC=2\\sqrt2$ and legs $EF=FC=2$, area $\\frac12\\cdot2\\cdot2=2$. Then $AFED=49-2=47$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 47**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "geometry"
    ],
    "difficulty": 2,
