        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "5"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "more than 5"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Last digits",
        "body": "The terms are $1,3,9,33,153,\\ldots$. For $n\\ge5$, $n!$ ends in 0, so every term from $1!+\\cdots+4!=33$ on ends in 3. A perfect square never ends in 3. The only squares are 1 and 9: two.\n\n**Answer: (B) 2**"
      }
    ],
