    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Find the centre",
        "body": "The triangle has sides 12, 12, 6, so its height is $\\sqrt{144-9}=3\\sqrt{15}$. The centre lies on the axis of symmetry at distance $r$ from each vertex, hence at distance $3\\sqrt{15}-r$ from the midpoint of the base. Then $r^2=3^2+(3\\sqrt{15}-r)^2$ gives $6\\sqrt{15}\\,r=144$, so $r=\\frac{24}{\\sqrt{15}}=\\frac{8\\sqrt{15}}5$.\n\n**Answer: (A)**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Area formula",
        "body": "$R=\\frac{abc}{4K}$ with $K=\\frac12\\cdot6\\cdot3\\sqrt{15}=9\\sqrt{15}$: $R=\\frac{864}{36\\sqrt{15}}=\\frac{24}{\\sqrt{15}}=\\frac{8\\sqrt{15}}5$.\n\n**Answer: (A)**"
      }
    ],
