    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Digits must be 1, 1, p",
        "body": "A product of three digits is prime only if two digits are 1 and the third is a one-digit prime $p\\in\\{2,3,5,7\\}$. For each $p$ the digits $1,1,p$ can be arranged in 3 ways. Total $4\\times3=12$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 12**"
