        "text": "6"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "5"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Factorise",
        "body": "$n^5-n=n(n^2-1)(n^2+1)=(n-1)n(n+1)(n^2+1)$ is divisible by the product of three consecutive integers $(n-1)n(n+1)$, hence by 2 and by 3, so by 6. Of the options 1, 2, 3, 6, 5 the number 6 is the largest, so it is the answer. (In fact $n^5-n$ is always divisible by 30, but 30 is not offered.)\n\n**Answer: (D) 6**"
      }
